A member-access chain is never split at a `:` boundary when a line
wraps: the break lands after the comma before the chain and the whole
`oConfiguration:database:timeout` moves to the continuation line
(fmt.atomic_property_chains, issue #16).
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE Connect;
:PARAMETERS oConfiguration;
:DECLARE sValue;
sValue := SomeFunctionWithLongName(oConfiguration:database:connectionString, oConfiguration:database:timeout);
:RETURN sValue;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE Connect;
	:PARAMETERS oConfiguration;
	:DECLARE sValue;
	sValue := SomeFunctionWithLongName(oConfiguration:database:connectionString,
		oConfiguration:database:timeout);
	:RETURN sValue;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
4:11-4:35 warning direct_procedure_call: 'SomeFunctionWithLongName' is not a known built-in function or in-file procedure. If it is a custom procedure, dispatch it via DoProc/ExecFunction; if it is a legacy vendor built-in, this call is valid as written.
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
4:11-4:35 warning direct_procedure_call: 'SomeFunctionWithLongName' is not a known built-in function or in-file procedure. If it is a custom procedure, dispatch it via DoProc/ExecFunction; if it is a legacy vendor built-in, this call is valid as written.
